a "card" is a thing
a "column" is a list of cards

solitaire is an app where:
	// Klondike solitaire:  deal seven columns, then build four foundations, ace to king, one suit each.

	// The seven piles cards are played on
	- its "columns" is a new list of columns
	// How many moves so far
	- its "moves" is 0
	- to start a new game:
		- shortcut meta+N
		set its moves to 0
	- to undo the last move:
		- shortcut meta+Z
		- enabled when its moves > 0
		set its moves to its moves - 1
	- on mouse down:
		// A press a card passed on.
		print "pressed"
	- to draw it:
		<ui-toolbar />
		<ui-text>{its moves} moves</ui-text>
		for each column in its columns
			<ui-segment>{draw the column}</ui-segment>

a "score page" is a page where:
	// A page that lists games, best first.
	- its "scores" is a new list of numbers

leaderboard is a score page where:
	// The ten best games, fastest first.
	- to draw it:
		<ui-header>High scores</ui-header>
		for each score in its scores
			<ui-text>{the score}</ui-text>
